  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize 'Badugi' potential. If you are dealt 3 cards of the same suit, you MUST discard two of them, leaving you with a very weak 2-card hand.\n\nSnowing (Bluffing): In a triple draw game, you can 'Pat' (discard 0 cards) to make opponents think you already have a powerful Badugi, forcing them to fold or play defensively.\n\nRange Analysis: If an opponent draws only 1 card on the first draw and then stands pat on the second, they almost certainly have a completed Badugi. If that Badugi is an 8-high or better, you should fold unless you are drawing to a 7-high or better.",
    Player: "Prioritize 'Badugi' potential. If you are dealt 3 cards of the same suit, you MUST discard two of them, leaving you with a very weak 2-card hand.\n\nSnowing (Bluffing): In a triple draw game, you can 'Pat' (discard 0 cards) to make opponents think you already have a powerful Badugi, forcing them to fold or play defensively.\n\nRange Analysis: If an opponent draws only 1 card on the first draw and then stands pat on the second, they almost certainly have a completed Badugi. If that Badugi is an 8-high or better, you should fold unless you are drawing to a 7-high or better.",
